**[[ description ]]** `[[ dist_name ]]` is a package for
[canVODpy](https://canvodpy.eu/), an open Python ecosystem for
GNSS-Transmissometry (GNSS-T) canopy VOD retrievals. canVODpy works fully
without it.

## Layout

This repository is built like
[canvodpy-extensions](https://github.com/TUW-GEO/canvodpy-extensions),
reduced to one package:

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `packages/[[ dist_name ]]/` | The package: `src/canvod/[[ module_name ]]/`, tests, its own `pyproject.toml`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` |
| `docs/` | The docs site (Zensical); the package's pages are `docs/packages/[[ short_name ]]/` and `docs/api/[[ dist_name ]].md` |
| `release-notes/` | marimo notebooks, one per minor or major release |
| `tools/`, `scripts/` | The checks CI and the hooks run, the agent git guard |
| `.github/` | CI workflows, issue and pull request templates, Dependabot |

[% if target != 'standalone' %]The package is meant to move into [% if target == 'extensions' %]canvodpy-extensions[% else %]canvodpy[% endif %]
later: [MOVING.md](MOVING.md) says how.
[% endif %]

## Installation

`[[ dist_name ]]` is not on PyPI. Install a release from its git tag:

```bash
uv add "[[ dist_name ]] @ git+[[ repo_url ]]@[[ dist_name ]]-v0.1.0#subdirectory=packages/[[ dist_name ]]"
```

canVODpy requires Python 3.14.

## Development setup

You need [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and [just](https://github.com/casey/just).

```bash
git clone [[ repo_url ]].git
cd [[ repo_name ]]
just sync         # one .venv, plus the pre-commit, commit-msg and pre-push hooks
just labels       # once per repository: the GitHub labels the issue forms use
```

```bash
just --list       # all commands
just check        # ruff lint + format, ty, agent docs check
just test         # all tests
just docs         # preview the docs site
```

[% if not ci_enabled %]
The GitHub Actions workflows are off: they run only when started by hand,
since private repositories pay for Actions minutes. See "Continuous
integration" in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).
[% endif %]

